BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-lock-plan@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260605
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260606
SUMMARY:MiM DUE: Lock the stack + Aug/Sept recording dates with Carla
DESCRIPTION:The gate that starts everything. Confirm the build with Carla
  and lock the dates.\n\nDO\n- Walk Carla through the six-pager (mim-podc
 ast-roadmap.pdf).\n- Confirm the four-tool stack and the ~$1\,700 two-ki
 t hardware spend.\n- Lock the eight Tue/Thu recording slots on both cale
 ndars.\n- Confirm the split: Rich = logistics\, Carla = guest slate.\n\n
 RIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- Stack approved\; 8 slots on both calendars\; guest-s
 late ownership confirmed with Carla.\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (paste into Cla
 ude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\, the AES podcast: a remo
 te\, two-host video interview show that turns Amazon's internal operatin
 g mechanisms into playbooks any company can use (tagline 'Day 1 Energy f
 or Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\; Carla owns the guest s
 late. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in this calendar event (above) ar
 e your brief for this step. Use them. Then do this: We are at STEP 1: lo
 ck the stack and dates. Draft a 5-line confirmation message to Carla in 
 Rich's voice summarizing the stack\, the cost\, the Aug/Sept recording d
 ates\, and the logistics/guest-slate split.\n\nFULL PROJECT SPEC (option
 al\, for deep context): https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rwsmith96/mech
 anisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM DUE: Lock the stack + Aug/Sept recording dates with Carla
TRIGGER:-P2D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-guest-slate@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260620
SUMMARY:MiM DUE: First 4 guests identified + invites out (Carla)
DESCRIPTION:Carla's first deliverable: seed the guest slate.\n\nDO\n- Nam
 e the first 4 guests for the launch block and their order.\n- Send warm 
 invites with the Calendly booking link for the Aug 25+ slots.\n- Aim for
  a full 6-8 slate by early July.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- 4 names chosen\;
  4 warm invites sent\; a 6-8 guest slate forming.\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (p
 aste into Claude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\, the AES po
 dcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that turns Amazon's inte
 rnal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company can use (tagline 'D
 ay 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\; Carla own
 s the guest slate. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in this calendar eve
 nt (above) are your brief for this step. Use them. Then do this: We are 
 at STEP 2: guest-slate kickoff (Carla owns). Draft a warm\, peer-to-peer
  guest-invite template (subject + 6-8 lines): the show in one line\, the
  ask (75-min remote video)\, and a placeholder for the Calendly link.\n\
 nFULL PROJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.githubuser
 content.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
