BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-order-kits@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260702
SUMMARY:MiM DUE: Order both hardware kits (Rich)
DESCRIPTION:Order two identical kits (~$850 each) so they arrive together
  and stay matched. Pulled to Jul 1 from Jul 10 to absorb back-order risk
  on the long-lead items.\n\nDO\n- Order both kits in one pass\; add a sp
 are XLR cable.\n- Ship one to Rich (San Diego)\, one to Carla (Seattle a
 rea).\n- Target arrival before late July\; if any item is back-ordered\,
  sub the nearest equivalent now.\n\nBUY / HAVE READY\n- Shure MV7+ (blac
 k\, USB-C) $279 - shure.com or B&H\n- Logitech MX Brio 4K $199 - logitec
 h.com\n- Elgato Key Light Neo $99 - elgato.com\n- Sony MDR-7506 headphon
 es $100 - any pro-audio retailer\n- RODE PSA1+ boom arm $126 - rode.com\
 n- Reflection filter / acoustic foam ~$50 - Amazon (TONOR / TroyStudio)\
 n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- Two identical kits ordered\; arriving before late
  July\; no item silently back-ordered past Jul 25.\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (
 paste into Claude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\, the AES p
 odcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that turns Amazon's int
 ernal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company can use (tagline '
 Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\; Carla ow
 ns the guest slate. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in this calendar ev
 ent (above) are your brief for this step. Use them. Then do this: We are
  at STEP 3: order hardware. Confirm the kit list and current prices/link
 s\, flag any out-of-stock item with the nearest equivalent\, and produce
  one ordered shopping list with direct buy links for both kits.\n\nFULL 
 PROJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.githubuserconten
 t.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM DUE: Order both hardware kits (Rich)
TRIGGER:-P2D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-guest-gate@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260724
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260725
SUMMARY:MiM GATE: 3+ guests confirmed and BOOKED before the spend
DESCRIPTION:Hard go/no-go gate. The slate is the critical path\, so it ge
 ts a gate of its own.\n\nDO\n- Confirm at least 3 guests are BOOKED in C
 alendly (not just invited) for the sprint.\n- Carla curates names + warm
  intros\; Rich executes the outreach\, chasing\, and booking off the sha
 red list.\n- If short of 3\, hold the sprint start or plan to open with 
 hosts-only evergreens.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- 3+ guests booked into real
  Aug/Sept slots\; Rich has made the go/no-go call on the sprint.\n\nASSI
 STANT PROMPT (paste into Claude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Moti
 on\, the AES podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that turn
 s Amazon's internal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company can 
 use (tagline 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logist
 ics\; Carla owns the guest slate. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in th
 is calendar event (above) are your brief for this step. Use them. Then d
 o this: We are at the GUEST GATE. Help me check we have 3+ guests booked
 \, draft chase notes to any invited-but-unbooked guests\, and decide go 
 / no-go on starting the Aug 25 sprint.\n\nFULL PROJECT SPEC (optional\, 
 for deep context): https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rwsmith96/mechanism
 s-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
