BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-assemble-kits@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260727
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260728
SUMMARY:MiM DUE: Both kits assembled + bench-tested
DESCRIPTION:Build and bench-test both kits before the test run.\n\nDO\n- 
 Assemble both kits\; mount the MV7+ on the PSA1+ arm.\n- Install the Shu
 re Motiv app\; set Auto Level on\, light denoise\, reverb OFF.\n- Confir
 m mic\, webcam\, light\, and headphones work on each machine.\n\nRIGHT L
 OOKS LIKE\n- Both kits built and bench-tested\; Motiv settings applied o
 n each machine.\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (paste into Claude)\nYou are helping
  run Mechanisms in Motion\, the AES podcast: a remote\, two-host video i
 nterview show that turns Amazon's internal operating mechanisms into pla
 ybooks any company can use (tagline 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Gro
 wth'). Rich owns logistics\; Carla owns the guest slate. The DO list and
  RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in this calendar event (above) are your brief for this
  step. Use them. Then do this: We are at STEP 4: assemble + bench-test t
 he kits. Give me a 10-minute setup checklist for the MV7+ (USB-C mode + 
 Motiv settings)\, the MX Brio\, Key Light Neo placement (45 degrees\, sl
 ightly above eye level)\, and a 30-second test-recording to confirm each
  kit.\n\nFULL PROJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.gi
 thubusercontent.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-co
 ntext.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
