BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-learn-descript@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:MiM DUE: Learn Descript on scrap footage (Rich)
DESCRIPTION:Build Descript muscle memory before the test run.\n\nDO\n- Ru
 n one full mock edit end to end on throwaway footage.\n- Import multitra
 ck\, Studio Sound 60-80%\, filler removal\, Automatic Multicam\, caption
 s\, one vertical clip\, export to spec.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- One full 
 mock edit done\; export reads -14 LUFS / -1.0 dBTP at 1080p/30fps.\n\nAS
 SISTANT PROMPT (paste into Claude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Mo
 tion\, the AES podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that tu
 rns Amazon's internal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company ca
 n use (tagline 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logi
 stics\; Carla owns the guest slate. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in 
 this calendar event (above) are your brief for this step. Use them. Then
  do this: We are at STEP 5: learn Descript. Walk me\, in order\, through
  one full mock edit of a 5-minute multitrack remote interview with the e
 xact spec settings (Studio Sound 60-80%\, filler removal\, Automatic Mul
 ticam\, captions\, one 9:16 clip\, export -14 LUFS / -1.0 dBTP at 1080p/
 30fps). Flag the top 3 beginner mistakes as we go.\n\nFULL PROJECT SPEC 
 (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rwsmith
 96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM DUE: Learn Descript on scrap footage (Rich)
TRIGGER:-P2D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-day1-setup@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T110000
SUMMARY:MiM: Day-1 software setup (one time)
DESCRIPTION:One-time account setup. Do it once\, never touch again.\n\nDO
 \n- Create the 4 accounts on annual billing (Riverside Pro\, Descript Cr
 eator\, Transistor Pro\, Calendly Standard).\n- In Riverside\, enable 'E
 xport to Descript' (email Riverside support now if the button is missing
 ).\n- Connect the YouTube channel inside Transistor (document the manual
 -upload fallback if it won't connect).\n- Publish a 60-second TRAILER no
 w and submit the RSS feed to Apple Podcasts Connect + Spotify for Creato
 rs\, so directory review (days\, sometimes weeks) clears well before lau
 nch.\n- Run one private/unlisted end-to-end test episode: Transistor -> 
 confirm Apple/Spotify ingest + YouTube auto-post actually fire.\n- Build
  the Calendly 'Recording' event (75 min\, 15-min buffers\, Riverside lin
 k as location\, 3 intake questions)\; confirm the invite carries the lin
 k and the prep doc resolves view-only.\n- Write the guest prep one-pager
  (Google Doc\, view-only).\n- Set up the shared master-asset cloud folde
 r (Drive/Dropbox)\, one folder per episode.\n- Add both Rich and Carla a
 s admins on each account where allowed\; record logins in a credentials 
 note.\n- Confirm editor lanes: Rich owns the cut/multicam/export\; Carla
  owns clip selection + caption QA + guest-clip send.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE
 \n- Accounts live + both admins\; trailer published and feeds submitted 
 for early review\; private end-to-end publish proven\; YouTube connected
 \; Calendly + prep doc verified\; shared asset folder ready.\n\nASSISTAN
 T PROMPT (paste into Claude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\,
  the AES podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that turns Am
 azon's internal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company can use 
 (tagline 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\
 ; Carla owns the guest slate. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in this c
 alendar event (above) are your brief for this step. Use them. Then do th
 is: We are at STEP 6: Day-1 software setup. Give me an ordered runbook w
 ith the exact click-path for each task\, the trailer + private-test-epis
 ode procedure\, the precise Calendly 'Recording' fields\, and the full t
 ext of the guest prep one-pager (include a one-line audio+video reuse co
 nsent).\n\nFULL PROJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.
 githubusercontent.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-
 context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM: Day-1 software setup (one time)
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-test-run@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T094500
SUMMARY:MiM: Full test run (Rich + Carla + stand-in guest)
LOCATION:Riverside studio link (paste the persistent studio URL here once
  created)
DESCRIPTION:Prove the whole chain AND rehearse the real failure modes bef
 ore the first marquee guest. Costs nothing to break here.\n\nDO\n- Rich 
 + Carla + a stand-in on a RANDOM laptop with a default webcam (rehearse 
 the degraded guest\, not the happy path).\n- Mid-record\, have the stand
 -in close the tab and rejoin\; confirm their local track survived.\n- Co
 nfirm every participant's tracks upload to 100%\; rehearse the transcode
 -to-CFR step on the guest track.\n- Export to Descript\; confirm each pe
 rson lands as a SEPARATE track\; verify lip-sync at the END of the take.
 \n- Confirm 30fps everywhere\; export reads -14 LUFS / -1.0 dBTP.\n\nRIG
 HT LOOKS LIKE\n- Chain proven AND a disconnect/rejoin + degraded-guest +
  CFR-transcode rehearsed. Lip-sync clean at the end.\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT
  (paste into Claude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\, the AES
  podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that turns Amazon's i
 nternal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company can use (tagline
  'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\; Carla 
 owns the guest slate. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in this calendar 
 event (above) are your brief for this step. Use them. Then do this: We a
 re at STEP 7: full test run. Give me a 10-minute test-run script that de
 liberately rehearses a degraded guest\, a mid-record disconnect/rejoin\,
  and the transcode-to-CFR fix\, plus a pass/fail checklist for the chain
  (100% upload\, separate-track export\, end-of-take lip-sync\, -14 LUFS 
 / -1.0 dBTP\, 30fps)\, and exactly what to do if any check fails.\n\nFUL
 L PROJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.githubusercont
 ent.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM: Full test run (Rich + Carla + stand-in guest)
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM: Full test run (Rich + Carla + stand-in guest)
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
