BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mim-record-ep01@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260825T104500
SUMMARY:MiM: Record Ep01 (guest TBD)
LOCATION:Riverside studio link (paste the persistent studio URL here once
  created)
DESCRIPTION:Mechanisms in Motion\, Episode 01. 105-min block: 15 setup + 
 75 record + 15 buffer. The guest's local track is the one irreplaceable 
 asset\; protect it (upload marshal + archive below).\n\nDO\n- T-minus 5 
 min\, BEFORE the guest joins: both hosts confirm MV7+ selected\, 'separa
 te tracks / local recording' ON\, and QuickTime backup rolling. If any i
 s unconfirmed\, fix it before admitting the guest.\n- Headphones on for 
 everyone (kills echo).\n- Hit Record\; say the slate ('Episode N\, take 
 1')\; pause 3 seconds silent for sync.\n- Record ~60 min of conversation
 . If a guest's audio is rough\, ask them live to move closer\, turn off 
 fans/AC\, and put on headphones.\n- UPLOAD MARSHAL: one host's only end-
 of-session job is to watch EVERY track (including the GUEST's) to 100% i
 n the Riverside dashboard. The other host handles the goodbye. The guest
  is NOT released until the marshal calls 'clear.'\n- If a track is missi
 ng or stalls\, do NOT end the call: keep the guest on while it re-upload
 s\; if it can't\, rebook on the spot while you have them.\n- Archive imm
 ediately: both QuickTime backups + the Riverside download go to the shar
 ed cloud folder 'MiM-EpNN-Guest-YYYY-MM-DD/' before any editing.\n\nRIGH
 T LOOKS LIKE\n- Clean separate local tracks captured\; slate + 3-sec syn
 c pause\; GUEST track confirmed 100% before release\; Ep01 archived to t
 he shared cloud folder\; edit started within 48 hours.\n\nASSISTANT PROM
 PT (paste into Claude)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\, the A
 ES podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that turns Amazon's
  internal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company can use (tagli
 ne 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\; Carl
 a owns the guest slate. The DO list and RIGHT LOOKS LIKE in this calenda
 r event (above) are your brief for this step. Use them. Then do this: We
  are recording Episode 01 today. Before we start\, quiz me on the record
 -day non-negotiables (T-minus mic/local-recording/QuickTime check\, head
 phones\, slate + sync pause\, upload marshal confirms the GUEST track to
  100% before release\, archive to the shared folder). After the session\
 , remind me to archive and to start the edit within 48 hours.\n\nFULL PR
 OJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.githubusercontent.
 com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM: Record Ep01 (guest TBD)
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:MiM: Record Ep01 (guest TBD)
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
